# Database & RLS

- Postgres 16 is the system of record. Every tenant-scoped table carries a `tenant_id`
  column and an RLS policy — no table that holds job/user data is created without one.
- Migrations are expand/contract, applied before deploy: add nullable → backfill → make
  required/drop old, each as a separate deployable step. Never a single breaking migration.
- Treat `docs/architecture/data-model.md` as the canonical schema reference. Propose a
  schema change there (or open/update an ADR if it's structural) before writing the
  migration, not after.
- Never log row-level query results. Logs may reference a row by id, never its contents.
